WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.212
A transcription factor seen in a static structure seems

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:08.391
to invite a drug. In the cell, it inhabits shifting

00:00:08.391 --> 00:00:09.227
regulatory assemblies.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.146
A purified protein fragment can look druggable, while

00:00:20.146 --> 00:00:23.842
the living regulatory complex occupies many shapes and

00:00:23.842 --> 00:00:26.614
partnerships that a crystal cannot freeze.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.771
The therapeutic hypothesis should identify the

00:00:36.771 --> 00:00:39.538
disease-sustaining transcription-factor state and what

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:43.965
biological transition a ligand is supposed to cause.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.323
A thermal-shift curve or impressive affinity does not

00:00:52.323 --> 00:00:56.195
establish a change in transcriptional function or a

00:00:56.195 --> 00:00:57.163
therapeutic phenotype.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.989
Engagement, conformation, chromatin occupancy and

00:01:05.989 --> 00:01:09.543
cellular response must be linked through experiments

00:01:09.543 --> 00:01:12.590
that can also disprove the claim.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.078
The intervention must specify which state is altered

00:01:21.078 --> 00:01:24.706
and which readout establishes the change. A promising

00:01:24.706 --> 00:01:26.974
pocket is a starting hypothesis.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.204
Belzutifan, TEAD inhibitors and mutant-p53 reactivation

00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:39.959
illustrate distinct modes of controlling regulatory

00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:43.713
state rather than a universal method.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.686
Drug design should interrogate the living regulatory

00:01:49.686 --> 00:01:53.846
state instead of falling in love with an isolated

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:54.309
conformation.
